# DMR-0NN: <verb> <concrete behavior or outcome>
#
# Name the behavior, not the review tool or activity. Avoid subjects such as
# "address comments", "misc fixes", "sync changes", or "update files".
#
# Problem
# <Trigger, incorrect behavior, and its impact.>
#
# Changes
# - <path>: <what changed and why; group closely related paths if clearer>.
#
# Validation
# - <exact command or named gate>: <result, including failures and skips>.
# - <bug fix>: <regression that failed before and passes after>.
#
# Compatibility and provenance
# <Public behavior, preserved contracts, migration/rollback, or known limits.>
# <For imports/vendors: source PR, merged SHA/release, generation command,
#  exact-tree proof, and any intentionally retained integration overlays.>
#
# References
# <Card/issue/PR IDs and durable evidence links where relevant.>
#
# Scale the body to the change. Keep only useful sections; never invent
# validation, imply an unfinished gate passed, or leave placeholders in it.
